1
00:06:14,285 --> 00:06:20,285
Ferrari is a history, drama film directed by Michael Mann.

2
00:12:28,571 --> 00:12:34,571
Set during the summer of 1957.

3
00:18:42,857 --> 00:18:48,857
Ex-racecar driver, Enzo Ferrari, is in crisis.

4
00:24:57,142 --> 00:25:03,142
Bankruptcy stalks the company he and his wife, Laura,
built from nothing ten years earlier.

5
00:31:11,428 --> 00:31:17,428
Their tempestuous marriage struggles with the mourning for
one son and the acknowledgement of another.

6
00:37:25,714 --> 00:37:31,714
Enzo Ferrari, played by Adam Driver.

7
00:43:40,000 --> 00:43:46,000
Laura Ferrari, played by Penélope Cruz.

8
00:49:54,285 --> 00:50:00,285
Lina Lardi, played by Shailene Woodley.

9
00:56:08,571 --> 00:56:14,571
Alfonso de Portago, played by Gabriel Leone.

10
01:02:22,857 --> 01:02:28,857
Linda Christian, played by Sarah Gadon.

11
01:08:37,142 --> 01:08:43,142
Peter Collins, played by Jack O'Connell.

12
01:14:51,428 --> 01:14:57,428
Ferrari is a 2023 American biographical sports drama film directed
by Michael Mann and written by Troy Kennedy Martin.

13
01:21:05,714 --> 01:21:11,714
Based on the 1991 biography Enzo Ferrari: The Man, the Cars, the Races, the Machine by motorsport journalist Brock Yates, the film follows the personal and professional struggles
of Enzo Ferrari, the Italian founder of the car manufacturer Ferrari, during the summer of 1957 as Scuderia Ferrari prepares to compete in the 1957 Mille Miglia.

14
01:27:20,000 --> 01:27:26,000
Adam Driver portrays the titular subject, and Penélope Cruz, Shailene Woodley, Sarah
Gadon, Gabriel Leone, Jack O'Connell, and Patrick Dempsey co-star.

15
01:33:34,285 --> 01:33:40,285
Ferrari was selected to compete for the Golden Lion at the 80th Venice
International Film Festival, premiering on August 31, 2023.

16
01:39:48,571 --> 01:39:54,571
The film was originally set to premiere on the streaming service Showtime, but it was
eventually released in the United States theatrically on December 25, 2023, by Neon.

17
01:46:02,857 --> 01:46:08,857
The film received generally positive reviews from critics and was named one
of the top 10 films of 2023 by the National Board of Review.

18
01:52:17,142 --> 01:52:23,142
The film underperformed at the box office, grossing only $43
million worldwide against a $95 million budget.

19
01:58:31,428 --> 01:58:37,428
The film explores themes of husband wife relationship,
biography, based on true story, racing, 1950s.

20
02:04:45,714 --> 02:04:51,714
The tone is emotional.
